# The live loop's schedule (issue #19). Install with:
#
#   crontab -l > /tmp/current && cat /path/to/epl_predictor/deploy/crontab >> /tmp/current \
#     && crontab /tmp/current
#
# then replace __ROOT__ with the absolute path of the clone on this Pi (`pwd` inside it).
#
# WHY THESE TIMES. A Prediction Round's sealing window opens at its As-Of Instant — midnight at
# the start of the Tuesday or Friday it anchors to — and shuts at its first kickoff (ADR 0005).
# Football-Data samples the pre-match odds on the *afternoon* of that day, so the window has two
# ends that are both real: fire at midnight and the odds the Market Line needs do not exist yet;
# fire after the first kickoff and the store refuses the round outright. 16:00 is after the
# sample and comfortably before a 19:45 or 20:00 first kickoff.
#
# WHY TWICE. 18:30 is a retry, and it is free: sealing is idempotent inside a round, so the second
# fire finds the round already sealed, writes nothing, adds no commit — and still pushes, which is
# the whole point. The run that seals a round is exactly the run that may have been unable to
# reach the network, and a sealed round that never left this Pi is not evidence of anything.
#
# WHY score ON THE SAME DAYS. A Tuesday round is played Tuesday to Thursday and a Friday round
# Friday to Monday, so each morning fire scores the round that has just finished, hours before the
# next one is sealed. It ingests the Live Season and rebuilds the match table itself, so nothing
# else has to run first.
#
# CRON_TZ is what makes 16:00 mean 16:00 in London on a Pi whose own clock is not.
#
# DO NOT ASSUME IT WORKS. It was written here believing Debian's cron honours it, and on the Pi this
# was first deployed to — Raspberry Pi OS, cron 3.0pl1-197 — it is **ignored**. Measured 28 Aug 2026
# by the probe in deploy/SETUP.md step 8: an entry at 16:29 under CRON_TZ=Europe/London did not fire
# at 11:29 EDT, and an entry at 11:32 fired at 11:32 EDT exactly. Cron read the system zone.
#
# Check before trusting it, because the consequence is NOT mild on a machine whose own zone is
# behind the UK. The comment here used to say it was: "the loop would fire outside the window and
# exit 0 having sealed nothing". That is true of a clock that runs early and false of one that runs
# late — on a Pi set to America/New_York these times land five hours after they read, so 18:30
# becomes 23:30 in London, past a 20:00 first kickoff, and the round is gone rather than deferred.
# Sealing nothing every week is exactly as quiet as having nothing to seal.
#
# What is still true: the window is judged in UK time by the code (epl.ledger.live.uk_now) whatever
# cron believes, so a wrong hour here cannot seal something *wrongly*. It can only miss it.
#
# If the probe shows CRON_TZ is ignored, apply SETUP.md step 8's fallback: convert the three times
# into the Pi's own zone and DELETE this line — leaving it while the times are already converted
# means a future cron that starts honouring it shifts them a second time.
CRON_TZ=Europe/London

# m  h  dom mon dow  command
  0  6  *   *   2,5  __ROOT__/deploy/run_live.sh score
  0 16  *   *   2,5  __ROOT__/deploy/run_live.sh seal --push
 30 18  *   *   2,5  __ROOT__/deploy/run_live.sh seal --push

# Nothing here fires more often than that, and nothing here runs `python -m epl.ledger backfill`.
# The Evaluation Window is over closed Seasons and must go on meaning the same thing from one week
# to the next; regenerating it on a timer would also have `backfill` rewrite Predictions this loop
# had sealed, which is ADR 0005's exact failure. The Live Season is sealed and scored, never
# backfilled (epl.windows).
